<mujoco model="kidney_dish">
  <!--
    A 7-inch stainless kidney dish (emesis basin), standing on a table.
    Dimensions in millimetres:

      overall        177.8 long, 108.0 wide, 33.6 to the rim
      basin floor    163.4 x 93.8, 33.0 deep
      lobe radius    38.0, concave notch 15.0
      wall flare     12 degrees from vertical, sheet gauge 0.6
      mass           125 g of 304 stainless

    CONFIRM WITH CALIPERS: scaled against a reference photograph using the
    122 mm syringe beside it, which landed on a catalogue size. The notch
    depth is from the photograph alone.

    TWO GEOMETRY GENERATIONS, and they must stay in step. `dish_visual` is the
    mesh and is never collided; the wall and floor boxes are collided and never
    rendered. The split is not optional: MuJoCo collides a mesh as its convex
    hull, and this shell encloses 3.4% of its own hull, so a mesh-collided dish
    is a solid bean with the basin filled in.

    The collision wall is 4.0 mm rather than the 0.6 mm gauge and grows outward
    from the visible inner face -- boxes at the true gauge tunnel. The floor
    strips overshoot the basin outline, which is safe only because they stay
    under the wall and are coplanar with the table. The floor plate reaches
    8 mm below the basin so a thin sheet cannot pass through; it sinks into the
    table harmlessly, MuJoCo filtering contacts between two static bodies.

    The body is mocap: immovable like the table, and re-posable per reset.

    Adding this dish raises the contact budget -- mjlab's lift-cube default of
    nconmax=55 overflows at >= 90 with an object resting in the basin.
  -->

  <default>
    <default class="collision">
      <geom contype="1" conaffinity="1" group="5" mass="0" rgba="0 0 0 0" />
    </default>
  </default>

  <asset>
    <texture
      name="kidney_dish_steel_texture"
      type="2d"
      file="../textures/ambientcg/basecolor_256/Metal009_Color.png"
    />
    <material
      name="kidney_dish_steel"
      texture="kidney_dish_steel_texture"
      rgba="1 1 1 1"
      specular="0.3"
      shininess="0.25"
      reflectance="0.0"
      texrepeat="1 1"
      texuniform="false"
    />
    <mesh name="kidney_dish_mesh" file="meshes/kidney_dish.obj" />
  </asset>

